## Why Tasks Cannot Be Parallelized

- Playback helper work depends on the client type and API mapping contract.
- The translate result control should prove the playback helper in the primary workflow before the history detail view reuses it.
- Running result and history UI work in parallel risks duplicate playback components, inconsistent loading/error states, and conflicts in shared client mapping.

## Shared Contract Surfaces

- `lib/types.ts`
- `lib/api.ts`
- shared playback helper or hook
- `app/translate.tsx`
- `app/history.tsx`

## Cross-Epic Gates

This epic depends on Epic 03's detail response shape and playback access verification. Epic 05 depends on the history detail control before final QA docs and runtime testing.

## Recommendation

Run this epic sequentially after Epic 03. Prefer one shared playback helper/control path instead of parallel UI implementations.
